he verdict -> after: when supplied, the recorded act names the verdict -> not the same: an act naming none no longer fails this criterion. Unchanged since 003 blessed it. It is the Done-when's \"`--verdict` stays optional and recorded\".\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-278 Detail -> before: scope and backing bounds, plus a held clause refusing a held re-attestation whose ledger names no accepted CLARITY verdict -> after: the same bounds, with the held clause retired into the lane rule -> not the same: the ledger-based held refusal leaves this row. Unchanged since 003 blessed it.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-246 Detail, Title, SR-Refs -> before: loop writers and the marker-armed step refuse held status moves, and the slot re-judges loop lanes -> after: a lane rider and squash path judge every lane by state, the bound-copy exception applies, the marker arm narrows to commits outside a lane, and SR-228 is a parent -> not the same: the subject moves from provenance to lane state. Unchanged since 003 blessed it. Its `TestRefs` now name TC-241 alone, which matches TC-278 no longer verifying it.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-241 Expected, Method, Verifies -> before: a held status change is refused where the loop commits and at the merge -> after: the lane rule's claims, exception, refusals, marker arm and not-judged cases, verifying SR-208, SR-228 and LLR-246 -> not the same: the verified set is rebuilt with the rule. Unchanged since 003 blessed it.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] LLR-249 Detail -> before: `acceptance_record.committed_status_moves(root, rev)` lists status moves -> after: `committed_status_moves(root, rev)` lists them -> not the same: the contract no longer fixes which module holds the function, so an implementation placed anywhere now satisfies a row the old text tied to one module. Ready to bless. Sitting 003's finding is answered. The row keeps its approved symbol verbatim, adds no name, and stays true across the module move this lane made.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-278 Expected, Method, Verif