08's bound-text clause and shares SR-178's comparison basis. LLR-246 owns the landing rule that reads the same identity, so the two rows do not overlap. TC-398's fourteen cases hold each clause, including the malformed cell at the act turn -> why it is ready: a contract in observable inputs, outcomes and refusals, with no `shall` and no symbol in its text, unchanged since 003.\n- [APPROVE] TC-398 -> the obligation: the digest's exclusions and invariance, the identity lines, their preservation through reservation and both outcome rewrites, and the held CLARITY act refused before launch on moved text or an absent or malformed identity -> what its chain shows: Expected is LLR-359 sentence for sentence, and every evidence node exists -> why it is ready: an observable Expected over existing cases, with Integration at Full honest for its git cases, unchanged since 003.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=2\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1788,"cache_read_input_tokens":497336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1788},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"690ff3f1-f560-44e0-a223-2b95fd33b5c1","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:42.303Z","request_id":"req_011CgKbSyqe8M7vYygCoF4rR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Uj6Gv6YjeWm2SVoZcS76yX":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-851\\docs\\reviews\\wi-851\\004-ADJUDICATE-d860906.md","content":"# WI-851 checkpoint sitting at d860906\n\n## amendment\n\nThis re-sits the whole set after sitting 003 (`003-ADJUDICATE-5a56d69.md`). That sitting blessed SR-208, SR-228, LLR-278, LLR-246 and TC-241, and did not bless LLR-249,