plementation placed anywhere now satisfies a row the old text tied to one module. Ready to bless. Sitting 003's finding is answered. The row keeps its approved symbol verbatim, adds no name, and stays true across the module move this lane made.\n- [MEANING+BLESS] TC-278 Expected, Method, Verifies -> before: Expected paraphrased LLR-278 with a held CLARITY permission, and it verified SR-178, SR-228, SR-208, LLR-278 and LLR-246 -> after: Expected states LLR-278's scope, backing, combined-act and carrier-path arms in plain words. Method adds the ledger-parse refusal, acts on trunk not re-read, and the carrier-path arms. Verifies is SR-178, LLR-278 and IF-091 -> not the same: the verified set narrows to LLR-278's own obligations. Ready to bless. All three of sitting 003's findings are answered:\n  - (1) \"the amendment scope\" and \"the re-attestation ledger reader\" replace the two function names;\n  - (2) \"Every id re-attested by an act the merge base does not hold\" gives the claim its antecedent in the cell itself;\n  - (3) the held-tier rows have left `Verifies`, and TC-241 holds them.\n\n  Note, not a finding: Method still carries the sentence \"The same retirement on a held rung is refused by row\", which is LLR-246's arm. Its case also sits in TC-241, so nothing is claimed falsely. A later edit could drop the sentence.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=7\n\n## first-approval\n\nLLR-359 and TC-398 are byte-identical to the text sitting 003 approved. Their parents (SR-178, and SR-208 as blessed above) state what they decompose, unchanged since 003. The re-sit touches only LLR-249 and TC-278, neither of which is in their chain's verification set. I approve both again, on 003's reasons.\n\n- [APPROVE] LLR-359 -> the obligation: one approved-text digest over a row's nonempty approved cells, with id and Status excluded, insensitive to the carrier and to empty versus absent. One judged-text identity line per shown row in the amendment brief. The identities written at reservation and kept through the accepted or failed rewrite. A held CLARITY re-attestation actable only when the accepted binding's identity equals the committed digest, so that an absent, malformed or unequal identity is refused before launch, naming the row -> what its chain shows: it decomposes SR-208's bound-text clause and shares SR-178's comparison basis. LLR-246 owns the landing rule that reads the same identity, so the two rows do not overlap. TC-398's fourteen cases hold each clause, including the malformed cell at the act turn -> why it is ready: a contract in observable inputs, outcomes and refusals, with no `shall` and no symbol in its text, unchanged since 003.\n- [APPROVE] TC-398 -> the obligation: the digest's exclusions and invariance, the identity lines, their preservation through reservation and both outcome rewrites, and the held CLARITY act refused before launch on moved text or an absent or malformed identity -> what its chain shows: Expected is LLR-359 sentence for sentence, and every evidence node exists -> why it is ready: an observable Expected over existing cases, with Integration at Full honest for its git cases, unchanged since 003.\n\nOUTCOME: APPROVE rows=2\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Uj6Gv6YjeWm2SVoZcS76yX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
